This product includes source code adapted from Articraft
([github.com/mattzh72/articraft](https://github.com/mattzh72/articraft)).

The vendored code is the run viewer's frontend: the three.js/URDF viewport and
joint controls (`viewer/web/src/components/viewer3d/`), the shared UI primitives
(`viewer/web/src/components/ui/`, `viewer/web/src/components/layout/`), the
trajectory inspector's turn renderer and parsers
(`viewer/web/src/components/inspector/`), and the small shared helpers under
`viewer/web/src/lib/`. Files modified for dycraft start with a header saying so,
and the files in those directories written for dycraft are listed in
`viewer/web/src/components/README.md`.

It is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, consistent with the
upstream license; the license text is in `LICENSE`.

---

This product includes documentation mirrored from cuRobo
([github.com/NVlabs/curobo](https://github.com/NVlabs/curobo),
[nvlabs.github.io/curobo](https://nvlabs.github.io/curobo/latest/)),
Copyright (c) 2023-2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES.

`animation/ik/curobo_docs/` holds an unmodified-in-substance copy of the cuRobo
v0.8.0 (cuRoboV2) documentation pages an `h.ik` script needs, converted from the
published HTML to Markdown by `animation/ik/fetch_curobo_docs.py`. The
conversion strips navigation chrome and permalink anchors; no content is
rewritten. Each file carries the URL it came from. It is vendored because a
dycraft run executes without network access, so the published site is
unreachable from inside one.

It is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, consistent with the
upstream license; the license text is in `LICENSE`.

---

This product does not include motion-capture data. `python -m dycraft.install
mocap` downloads the CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (mocap.cs.cmu.edu;
BVH conversion by B. Hahne, from github.com/una-dinosauria/cmu-mocap) and, with
`--dog` and the user's acceptance, the MANN dog captures
(github.com/sebastianstarke/AI4Animation, CC BY-NC 4.0).

`animation/mocap/libraries/mann_dog/index.txt` holds dycraft's own labels of
time spans in the MANN captures; the install copies it beside the captures.

---

The asset library is downloaded separately with `python -m dycraft.install
library`. Its characters keep their own licenses, listed per character in
the library's `catalog.json` and `CREDITS.md`, with the license texts in the
dataset's `LICENSES/` folder (huggingface.co/datasets/jefftan969/dycraft-assets).
They include CC BY 4.0, CC BY-SA 4.0, CC0, the MIT license (Microsoft
Rocketbox), the BSD 3-Clause license (the Unitree G1 description) and
Apache-2.0 (the Franka Panda description). Characters under CC BY-NC or
CC BY-NC-SA may be used for non-commercial purposes only.
